y default): new sessions can show the agent's mid-turn progress with an optional one-line title, enabled in the TUI `/experiments` or the web/Desktop settings' Lab section; set `[experimental] notify_user = true` or `KIMI_CODE_EXPERIMENTAL_NOTIFY_USER=1` to turn it on.\nL190:   * cite90†#4145 cite91†`242ac23` Thanks cite92†@wbxl2000 ! - Add `kimi app [path]` to open a new desktop chat in the current or specified directory.\nL191: \nL192:   * cite93†#4061 cite94†`20a2cea` Thanks cite95†@chengluyu ! - Cap the agent's in-turn wait for background tasks at 90 seconds (longer timeouts are no longer accepted), discourage repeated waits, and let a new message end the wait immediately.\nL193:   * cite96†#3998 cite97†`09af3b4` Thanks cite98†@tpoisonooo ! - Tower mode: a message sent while the agent is running aborts the in-progress turn and runs as its own turn.\nL194: \nL195:   * cite99†#4031 cite100†`33e368a` Thanks cite101†@Grapedge ! - Add sticky user message summaries in fullscreen mode; click a summary to jump to the original message.\nL196:   * cite102†#4074 cite103†`c9f01f0` Thanks cite98†@tpoisonooo ! - Tower mode: deterministic orchestration with TowerRebase and LLM-free status, goal/tower mutual exclusion, and workspace protection.\nL197: \nL198:   * cite104†#4059 cite105†`1f6f0b1` Thanks cite106†@7Sageer ! - Add the KIMI_CODE_TRUST_WORKSPACE environment variable to mark the workspace as trusted.\nL199: \nL200:   * cite107†#4165 cite108†`afd95f6` Thanks cite101†@Grapedge ! - Replace user skill cards with highlighted prompts and support Ctrl-S for skill prompts.\nL201: ### Patch Changes\nL202: \nL203:   * cite109†#4183 cite110†`c15638b` Thanks cite89†@RealKai42 ! - Cancel in-flight video uploads when a media read is interrupted.\nL204: \nL205:   * cite111†#4081 cite112†`06ebfc8` Thanks cite113†@sailist ! - Fix shifted turns and lost replies when a UserPromptSubmit hook injects text; hook JSON output without a \"message\" field is no longer added to the conversation.\nL206: \nL207:   * cite114†#4154 cite115†`419aced` Thanks cite106†@7Sageer ! - Fix media file reading on the first turn after resuming a session.\nL208:   * cite116†#4083 cite117†`f409caa` Thanks cite113†@sailist ! - Cron tasks from the source session no longer fire inside a forked session.\nL209: \nL210:   * cite118†#4152 cite119†`f0bc988` Thanks cite106†@7Sageer ! - Forked subagents now inherit the parent's available agent types, including custom agents.\nL211: \nL212:   * cite120†#4057 cite121†`a940f2f` Thanks cite122†@huangzheng2016 ! - Fix the permission mode switch in the goal-start approval prompt not taking effect on the v2 engine.\nL213:   * cite111†#4081 cite112†`06ebfc8` Thanks cite113†@sailist ! - Fix messages rendering out of place in sessions with a UserPromptSubmit hook.\nL214: \nL215:   * cite123†#4153 cite124†`7091138` Thanks cite89†@RealKai42 ! - Let the agent write one- or two-sentence progress notes between tool calls instead of bare status lines; in the experimental Updates panel (`KIMI_CODE_EXPERIMENTAL_NOTIFY_USER=1`), stop asking the agent to repost its mid-turn text as an update and remind it to post updates less often.\nL216:   * cite125†#4054 cite126†`4fbe065` Thanks cite89†@RealKai42 ! - Stop prompting the agent to send NotifyUser updates when a session is opened in a host that does not display them.\nL217: \nL218:   * cite127†#4091 cite128†`21406fb` Thanks cite113†@sailist ! - Omit max_tokens for models without an explicit output limit, fixing repeated 400 errors on strict serving stacks (e.g. bare vLLM) when the model's max output size is unknown.\nL219:   * cite129†#4184 cite130†`cbd7540` Thanks cite106†@7Sageer ! - Remove the never-implemented `executor = \"kaos\"` option from MCP stdio server configuration; configs using it now fail validation at load time.\nL220: \nL221:   * cite131†#2919 cite132†`0f052fe` Thanks cite133†@duyphan154 ! - Sanitize foreground Bash tool output so captured terminal escape sequences no longer change the host terminal state.\nL222:   * cite134†#4164 cite135†`3395f5b` Thanks cite122†@huangzheng2016 ! - Show a \"Shutting down\" status hint while shutdown hooks run during exit, and let a Ctrl+C during that window force an immediate exit instead of waiting for the hook timeout.\nL223: \nL224:   * cite136†#4033 cite137†`eec9bbd` Thanks cite101†@Grapedge ! - Feedback surveys now appear less often.\nL225: \nL226:   * cite138†#4160 cite139†`72fc1d0` Thanks cite140†@kimi-agent-bot ! - Show \"Working…\" in the status spinner while thinking.\nL227:   * cite141†#4056 cite142†`395d537` Thanks cite106†@7Sageer ! - Replace inline MCP commands in the workspace trust prompt with activation summaries and configuration paths for manual inspection.\nL228: \nL229:   * cite143†#4076 cite144†`e3bf50c` Thanks cite106†@7Sageer ! - Remove interruption reminders from the conversation when their interrupted turns are undone.\nL230: \nL231:   * cite99†#4031 cite100†`33e368a` Thanks cite101†@Grapedge ! - Replace the user message bullet ✨ with ❯.\nL232:   * cite145†#4221 cite146†`2e6821d` Thanks cite140†@kimi-agent-bot ! - web: Improved interactions and fixed known bugs.\nL233: \nL234: Assets 39\nL235: \nL236:   * cite147†kimi-code-darwin-arm64.tar.gz L237: \nL238: sha256:034b37fee68e242b8d1800470c502d5870602fb54e1597d99d20d9e9f3fa8f59\nL239: \nL240: 59.6 MB 2026-10-14T15:42:58Z\nL241: \nL242:   * cite148†kimi-code-darwin-arm64.tar.gz.sha256 L243: \nL244: sha256:1f9243f3168d79adcfdf050ef8100f0809cae528a172b7df19203fa27b73cb84\nL245: \nL246: 96 Bytes 2026-10-14T15:42:58Z\nL247: \nL248:   * cite149†kimi-code-darwin-arm64.zip L249: sha256:5a8f8867eac1967c7b3c79d2f98205665d6b2e281aa036c32a6faf57e910b67b\nL250: \nL251: 60.7 MB 2026-10-14T15:42:58Z\nL252: \nL253: 